data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"Let `p_o` be the fraction of items with equal labels. For each label, take the fraction of items\nrater A gave it and the fraction rater B gave it, multiply them, and sum over the label set; that\nsum is `p_e`. Then `kappa = (p_o - p_e) / (1 - p_e)`. The denominator is zero only when both raters\nused one label throughout, and that case needs its own error."},"hints_note":null}

